80071	80313	80064	80064	she	107	" It 'll be a real satisfaction to see that poor child wearing something decent for once . The way Marilla dresses her is positively ridiculous , that 's what , and I 've ached to tell her so plainly a dozen times . I 've held my tongue though , for I can see Marilla does n't want advice and she thinks she knows more about bringing children up than I do for all she 's an old maid . But that 's always the way . Folks that has brought up children know that there 's no hard and fast method in the world that 'll suit every child . But them as never have think it 's all as plain and easy as Rule of Three -- just set your three terms down so fashion , and the sum ? ll work out correct . But flesh and blood do n't come under the head of arithmetic and that 's where Marilla Cuthbert makes her mistake . I suppose she 's trying to cultivate a spirit of humility in Anne by dressing her as she does ; but it 's more likely to cultivate envy and discontent . I 'm sure the child must feel the difference between her clothes and the other girls ' . But to think of Matthew taking notice of it ! That man is waking up after being asleep for over sixty years . "
